From cc29f1ce0cb9460601ecc460f1ab7134f302f9c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:02:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(launcher): never launch a DOS-era executable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TES: Arena failed on every Play with `spawn
C:\Games\tes-arena\Arena106.exe EACCES` — a message that reads like a
permissions problem and sends players hunting through antivirus settings.

Arena106.exe is Bethesda's original 16-bit self-extracting installer,
which the freeware package ships beside the modern build. findExecutable
ranks every .exe the same and breaks ties by size, and the DOS blob is
the biggest file in the folder, so it became the stored launch target.
CreateProcess refuses a 16-bit image on 64-bit Windows and libuv reports
that refusal as EACCES.

Headers tell the two apart without running either: a modern binary's MZ
stub points at a "PE\0\0" signature, while DOS and 16-bit NE/LE images do
not. services/executableFormat.js reads that, and three places use it:

- findExecutable takes the best-ranked candidate that is actually a PE,
  so a DOS file can only win when it is the sole executable present.
- Play re-resolves a stored DOS launch target inside its own install
  folder before spawning, repairing existing installs without a
  reinstall, and reports the swap as launch_exe_repaired.
- GameLauncher refuses a DOS image outright with DOS_EXECUTABLE, so the
  player is told it needs DOSBox instead of seeing a spawn error.

EACCES from any other cause is now classified as SPAWN_EACCES and
explained as elevation or antivirus, rather than surfacing raw. Error
codes also survive spawnTrackedExe's re-wrap, which previously erased
them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FN6ATHFYk4mkNFeSvA2xwk
